          "y": "20.0",
          "w": "640"
        },
        "parms": "# bendout, xbendout and xbendout2 — the pitch wheel out\nA pitch-bend message carries 14 bits, as a coarse and a fine byte. bendout takes 0-127 with 64 at rest and sends it as the coarse byte, with the fine byte 0: the resolution bendin and midiparse report. xbendout takes all 14 bits, 0-16383 with 8192 at rest. xbendout2 takes the two bytes apart, as xbendin2 reports them.\nEach builds a message for midiout, and the left inlet sends it. The argument is the channel, counted from 0. How far a full bend goes is set on the synthesizer, often 2 semitones. midiout's argument is the output port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them. You hear something only when a synthesizer listens on that port.\nMax's bendout sends to a port itself, with the channel 1-16. Here the channel is counted from 0, and midiout sends.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
